  "details": "Users make crasher avatars by using a modded sdk to get past the performance limits the vrc sdk sets so they can upload avatars with high poly count/ particles, etc. I can click on a user in game and see their avatar performance stats in game so therefore, the game can detect that an avatar has a large amount of whatever it may be. I'm suggesting a second automatic check done after an avatar is uploaded that looks at how many polygons/particles an avatar has, because the data is in game may i remind you. and if it has too many polygons or too many particles, the avatar is not shown to people even if they hit show avatar or even better; the avatar is removed from the game.",
